Manually resizes the canvas element. With no parameters, the chart takes the size of its container. With explicit dimensions, it resizes to the given width and height. Returns 'this' for chainability.

```javascript
// Resizes & redraws to fill its container element
myLineChart.resize();
// => returns 'this' for chainability
// With an explicit size:
myLineChart.resize(width, height);
```

Resize the chart by changing the parent container's height and width. Note that the maintainAspectRatio option must be set to false for the height to resize correctly.

```javascript
chart.canvas.parentNode.style.height = '128px';
chart.canvas.parentNode.style.width = '128px';
```
